Firmware images and golden outputs of the hazard3 regression variants.

Every file here is GENERATED by ../build_firmware.py (do not edit by hand):

  <variant>/i_ram.hex      instruction RAM preload ($readmemh, one 32-bit word
  <variant>/d_ram.hex      per line); data RAM preload; both written by
                           ../elf2hex.py from the variant's RISC-V firmware
  <variant>/golden.tohost  the TOHOST stream the simulated CPU must send, as
                           tb/tb_hazard3.v prints it

Provenance and licence. The firmware is sw/mandelbrot.c of
verilator-hazard3-mandelbrot-testbench,
  https://github.com/verijit/verilator-hazard3-mandelbrot-testbench
  commit 9e768306a3cb03b9894aee609545fe3ed829d6be, file sw/mandelbrot.c
  "Copyright 2026 Can Joshua Lehmann", Apache License, Version 2.0,
unchanged, compiled with ../fw/rv32_tohost.c (derived from that repository's
sw/rv32.c) by clang/lld for RV32IMAC; the golden outputs come from the same
mandelbrot.c compiled natively with ../fw/native_tohost.c (derived from its
sw/native.c). These files are therefore covered by the Apache License,
Version 2.0, whose text is LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt at the root of this
repository. ../README.md says how they are built; ../variants.json records the
compilers, the commands and a SHA-256 of each file.
